From 38c999198911b4fee7ead53df5808094835745bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 01:43:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Show an outside job as a terminal and give the kit its menu
 page

A theme can now style a console: a monospaced window over the dimmed screen that an
outside job, such as the kit updater, fills through POST /job-console with its steps, a
gauge and a footer, or with a question of two answers. The screen takes every input, so
nothing starts under it while the job works, and it leaves by itself when the job goes
silent. The answer to a question goes to the updater as a request file: the menu runs no
installer. START gains a Canica page on consoles with the kit's updater: the version, how
it updates, a search, and the update that is ready.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
